-- Migration 101 (up): trending ranks the viewed slugs and keeps the published posts among them, and status, is_page and created_at are stored after content, so each check read the post's body. On a copy with 60k posts and 20k viewed slugs, the 30-day ranking took 21 s from a cold cache; /api/trending on johal.in answered in 6.8 s at p95. This index answers the check and the tie-break without the row: about 100 ms. NOTE: runMigrations executes line-by-line, so keep each statement on ONE line.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_articles_slug_listed ON articles(slug,status,is_page,created_at);
